  "description": "Sliding window primer: fixed vs variable windows, the expand/shrink/record template, window state (counts, distinct, missing, monotonic deque), atMost(K) for exactly K, and the TCP send window analogy, with Go, C++, Java and Python templates.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\"><span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">40 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Pattern primer</span><span class=\"chip\">Arrays &amp; strings</span><span class=\"chip\">O(n)</span></div>\r\n  <h1>Sliding Window</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Turn \"check every subarray\" from O(n&#178;) or O(n&#183;k) into one O(n) pass. Fixed windows, the expand / shrink / record template for variable windows, the window state you keep (sum, counts, distinct, a \"missing\" counter, a monotonic deque for the max), the atMost(K) trick for \"exactly K\", and the TCP send window you already know. Templates in Go, C++, Java and Python.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Go deeper:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-sliding-window-variants\">Sliding window variants: at most K, exactly K, shortest covering</a>, <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-monotonic-deque\">Monotonic deque</a>.</p>\r\n"
  },
